# Core MVP Principles — DO
- **Implement ONLY what the user explicitly asked for** - if details are ambiguous, ASK before proceeding
- **Touch ONLY files explicitly named** - if none are named, limit changes to a single appropriate file
- **Keep changes minimal** - prefer the shortest working solution over architecture
- **Avoid premature optimization** - focus on functionality first, optimization later
- **Keep output concise** - provide just what's necessary to fulfill the request

# Scope Restrictions — NEVER
- **Create new files, folders, configs, scripts, tests, types, comments, or docs** unless explicitly requested
- **Add dependencies, change build tooling, or adjust project settings** without explicit permission
- **Refactor existing code** beyond what's necessary for the request
- **Add "quality-of-life" improvements** that weren't requested
- **Implement additional features** beyond the scope of the request
- **Create abstractions or patterns** unless specifically asked

# Output Format — DO
- **First, provide ONLY the requested artifact(s) or edits** needed for the MVP (no extra commentary)
- **Then include a short "Next steps (optional)" section** with up to 5 bullet points describing recommended follow-ups
- **Keep the "Next steps" section brief** - no code or commands, just suggestions
- **Focus on the immediate need** rather than long-term architecture

# File Modification Restrictions — NEVER
- **Modify or generate code in:** tools/bruno/*
- **Touch files outside the scope** of the explicit request
- **Create unnecessary documentation** or README updates
- **Add configuration changes** unless specifically requested
- **Modify build processes** or deployment scripts

# Quality vs Scope Balance — DO
- **Prioritize working functionality** over perfect code structure
- **Use existing patterns** rather than creating new ones
- **Leverage existing utilities** instead of building new ones
- **Focus on the core requirement** rather than edge cases
- **Ask for clarification** when requirements are unclear

# Guardrails Checklist — VERIFY BEFORE FINALIZING
- [ ] **Scope matches request exactly** - no additional features
- [ ] **No extra files/dependencies/config** - only what was requested
- [ ] **Minimal diff/smallest working change** - efficient implementation
- [ ] **Only essential comments** - if any at all
- [ ] **Added "Next steps (optional)"** as plain bullets, no code
- [ ] **No scope creep** - stayed within explicit boundaries

